---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Character from '../components/Character.astro';

const org = 'https://github.com/Dash-AI-Tools';
const repo = `${org}/openspec-hud`;

const shots = [
  { src: '/openspec-hud/vertical.png', w: 1861, h: 813, alt: 'OpenSpec HUD docked as a side panel next to the Claude Code transcript, showing the change, the flow step, the context bar and usage', cap: 'Side panel: docked next to the transcript in the fullscreen UI at 110+ columns.' },
  { src: '/openspec-hud/horizontal.png', w: 1312, h: 612, alt: 'OpenSpec HUD as an inline bar above the Claude Code prompt', cap: 'Inline bar: above the prompt in the classic UI or a narrow terminal.' },
];

const shows = [
  ['Skill and step', 'The last OpenSpec skill (openspec-*) or command (/opsx:*, /openspec-*) you used, mapped to the flow step. With none, the step is inferred from the change\u2019s files: no tasks.md is propose, open tasks is apply, all done is verify.'],
  ['Change', 'The change named in your last /opsx:<cmd> <change>, otherwise the most recently edited change under openspec/changes/, archive excluded.'],
  ['Tasks', 'The current and next unchecked items in tasks.md, with done and total counts and what remains. They refresh after edits under openspec/, at each turn end and every 10 seconds.'],
  ['Agents', 'Subagents that are running right now, with their type, status and task description.'],
  ['MCP', 'The MCP server and tool being called, such as github \u00b7 get_me, shown only while the call is running.'],
  ['Context and usage', 'A context-window bar, tokens used out of the window, the 5-hour and 7-day rate-limit windows on subscriptions, and session cost.'],
];
---
<Base
  title="openspec-hud · Dash AI"
  description="openspec-hud is a Claude Code mod that shows your OpenSpec flow in a side panel: flow step, tasks, running agents, MCP calls, context and usage."
  current="hud"
>
  <section class="section page-top">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="plate tone-sky hud-plate">
        <Character kind="guest" class="hud-char" />
        <div class="hud-copy">
          <span class="quote">"OPENSPEC STATUS"</span>
          <span class="name">openspec-hud</span>
          <h1>Your OpenSpec flow, in a side panel next to the transcript.</h1>
          <p>A Claude Code mod that shows an <a href="https://github.com/Fission-AI/OpenSpec" rel="noopener">OpenSpec</a> HUD while you work: the flow step, your tasks, running agents, MCP calls, context and usage.</p>
          <ul class="proof" aria-label="At a glance"><li>Claude Code plugin</li><li>TypeScript</li><li>v0.3.0</li></ul>
          <p class="hud-cta">
            <a class="btn" href={repo} rel="noopener">View on GitHub
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 11h11.2l-4.6-4.6L12 5l7 7-7 7-1.4-1.4 4.6-4.6H4v-2Z"/></svg>
            </a>
            <a class="btn ghost" href="#install">Install</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint" id="see-it">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>See it working.</h2>
        <p>Two layouts, one HUD. Sections with nothing to show, such as no tasks or no running agent, are left out.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="term-shots">
        {shots.map((s) => (
          <figure class="term-shot">
            <div class="shot-scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Screenshot, scrolls sideways on small screens">
              <img src={s.src} alt={s.alt} width={s.w} height={s.h} decoding="async" />
            </div>
            <figcaption>{s.cap} <a href={s.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open full size</a></figcaption>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="what">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>What it shows.</h2></div>
      <ul class="spec">
        {shows.map(([h, p]) => (
          <li><h3>{h}</h3><p>{p}</p></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint" id="install">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>Install it.</h2></div>
      <div class="quick">
        <div class="notes">
          <p><strong>Run it at the Claude Code prompt.</strong> Answer <code>y</code> to add the marketplace, then pick a scope: User for every session, or Project for one repository. The panel opens right away.</p>
          <p><strong>Toggle it with <code>/openspec-hud</code>.</strong> Closing it with its close mark keeps it closed in later sessions until you open it again.</p>
          <p><strong>Docking needs the fullscreen UI.</strong> Set <code>"tui": "fullscreen"</code> in <code>~/.claude/settings.json</code> and use a terminal 110+ columns wide. Otherwise the panel opens inline above the prompt.</p>
          <p><strong>No license file yet.</strong> The repository does not include one at the time of writing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="code">
          <button class="copy" type="button" id="copy">Copy</button>
          <pre id="snippet"><code><span class="c"># at the prompt of a Claude Code session</span>
/plugin install openspec-hud --marketplace davidcp90/mods

<span class="c"># then, in a repo that uses OpenSpec</span>
/opsx:propose &lt;idea&gt;

<span class="c"># show or hide the panel</span>
/openspec-hud</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="shape">
    <div class="wrap about">
      <Character kind="egg" class="about-char" />
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Help shape it.</h2>
        <p>If you use OpenSpec with Claude Code, tell us what else you would want to see at a glance. It decides what gets built next.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="hud-cta">
        <a class="btn violet" href="/#next">Tell us what you need
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 11h11.2l-4.6-4.6L12 5l7 7-7 7-1.4-1.4 4.6-4.6H4v-2Z"/></svg>
        </a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href={repo} rel="noopener">Open the repo</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="close">
    <div class="close">
      <h2>Also from Dash AI: DocMyRepos.</h2>
      <Character kind="lead" />
      <a class="btn" href="/doc-my-repos/">See DocMyRepos
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 11h11.2l-4.6-4.6L12 5l7 7-7 7-1.4-1.4 4.6-4.6H4v-2Z"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</Base>
